Subject: [PATCH] Streaming tile: AirPlay's pairing controls

The Streaming dialog gains, under the AirPlay switch, "Ask new devices for
a code", and a "Paired devices (N)" button that lists the devices by name
and forgets one or all. Turning the code off asks first, since anyone on
the network could then stream; declining or backing out puts the tick
back.

None of this state is kept here. A streaming target can name its settings
provider, and the tile reads and changes the pairing state only through
it (for AirPlay, AirPlaySettingsProvider in the receiver's app), so the
tile shows what the receiver will actually do. A target without one, or
one that refuses, shows just its switch as before.

The four panel dialogs now share one helper that places them over the
panel, rather than four copies of it.

